=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play users/not-read ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: users/not-read$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. debian13, but visudo -c$
# rejects 90-cloud-init-users, so no rule is read: every change$
# refuses.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [?] User                 Unknown sudo config invalid$
$
  george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [?] Sudo                 Can't read$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  alice --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [?] Sudo                 Can't read$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select a user$
$
   1) george$
   2) alice$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
  User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [?] Sudo                 Can't read$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Grant admin rights   Let george become root$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1, 3 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# hardn can't read sudo's rules: its files don't check. Check$
# them with visudo -c, then try again.$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Managing: [george]$
$
  User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [?] Sudo                 Can't read$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Grant admin rights   Let george become root$
   3) SSH Keys             Add or remove SSH keys$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1, 3 or q]: 0$
$
# Manage User ##################################################$
$
  Select a user$
$
   1) george$
   2) alice$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [?] User                 Unknown sudo config invalid$
$
  george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [?] Sudo                 Can't read$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
  alice --------------------------------------------------------$
